    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence supports maintaining current AMZN positions without adding or exiting. Verified fundamentals are strong ($84.95B operating cash flow, $201.88B equity, ~$35B positive implied free cash flow) and the technical trend is clearly bullish with price above all key moving averages. However, the stock sits at its 60-day peak ($185.07) above the upper Bollinger Band ($184.48) with RSI at 66.38 approaching overbought, creating real short-term mean-reversion risk (downside to $173 or $147 vs. upside to $190-195). Critically, there is an information vacuum\u2014no income statement, revenue growth, net income, EPS, or segment margin data available to verify the growth narrative. Given the balanced evidence on both sides and the asymmetric risk profile at the peak, committing to either Buy or Sell would overreach. The prudent action is to hold existing positions, avoid chasing at the peak, and set a stop-loss alert below the 10 EMA ($180.76) for risk management.\n\n**Entry Price**: 180.76\n\n**Stop Loss**: 180.76\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain existing positions; do not add new exposure at the 60-day peak. If adding on a pullback toward the 10 EMA ($180.76) or 50 SMA ($173.16), size conservatively (no more than a standard position) given the information gaps.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
